My recommendation: Start with this approach using a list of dataclasses and a for loop. It's a relatively simple way to compare multiple measurements without needing complicated algorithms.

Later, you could improve it to rank locations from the closest match to the least similar match, rather than just finding locations within a certain tolerance.

how to add a header and a description
In Drafter, you can use Heading() and Text() to add a title and description to your webpage.

Example
@route
def index(state: State) -> Page:
    return Page(state, [
        Heading("Chesapeake Bay Water Identifier"),

        Text("Enter the temperature, pH, and salinity of your water sample to identify possible locations in the Chesapeake Bay."),

        LineBreak(),

        Text("Enter Temperature in Fahrenheit:"),
        TextBox("temperature"),

        Text("Enter pH:"),
        TextBox("pH"),

        Text("Enter Salinity in ppm:"),
        TextBox("salinity"),

        Button("Submit", submit)
    ])

