I can see a few issues in your code that are preventing the website from working as intended. Your overall structure is good, and using dataclasses for your Chesapeake Bay locations is a sensible approach!

Here are the main things I'd fix.

1. Your Submit button calls the wrong route
Currently, you have:

Button("Submit", submit)

But your process_matches() function is the one that actually compares the measurements.

Change it to:

Button("Submit", process_matches)

2. Fix your process_matches function
Your function currently expects three additional parameters:

def process_matches(state: State, temperature: str, pH: str, salinity: str)

You can simplify this by using the values stored in your State dataclass.

Since your text boxes use the same names as your State attributes, Drafter can update those attributes when the form is submitted.

Use:

@route
def process_matches(state: State) -> Page:

    temperature = float(state.temperature)
    pH = float(state.pH)
    salinity = float(state.salinity)

    matches = []

    for location in all_locations:
        if (abs(location.temperature - temperature) <= 2 and
            abs(location.pH - pH) <= 0.2 and
            abs(location.salinity - salinity) <= 3):

            matches.append(location.name)

    if len(matches) > 0:
        return Page(state, [
            Header("Possible Matches"),
            Text(", ".join(matches))
        ])

    else:
        return Page(state, [
            Header("No Matches Found"),
            Text("No matching locations were found.")
        ])

3. Fix your comments inside Page()
You have some comments written using triple quotation marks:

"""
LineBreak() creates a line tab on the website...
"""

These are actually multiline strings, not comments.

They can also cause syntax errors if you don't put commas between the components in your list.

Use # instead:

# LineBreak() creates a line break on the website.

You can use # for all your explanations throughout the program.

4. Correct your index function
Here is the corrected version:

@route
def index(state: State) -> Page:
    return Page(state, [
        Header("Where in the Bay?"),

        Text("Where in the bay is your sample from?"),

        Text("Input your information below regarding a sample from January of 2026 to generate possible locations!"),

        LineBreak(),

